+# Welcome code reuse after cancel and free delivery at 50 euro
+
+Two reports against the order service. Each is checked against the business rules in `README.md`,
+which is the reference.
+
+1. **Single-use code refused after a cancelled order (customer, Paolo).** Paolo placed an order with his
+   one-time welcome code, cancelled it the same day (wrong size), and the corrected order was refused
+   with "already used". The README says cancelling an order gives back its coupon, if the coupon was
+   single-use, so the corrected order should accept the code.
+   - Cause: `OrderService.place` records the use under the order's id (`ORD-0001`), but
+     `OrderService.cancel` gives the coupon back under the customer's name (`order.customer`). The
+     `giveBack` match never succeeds, so the code stays used.
+   - Fix: `cancel` in `src/orders.ts` gives the coupon back under `order.id`. The rest stays as it is.
+
+2. **Delivery charged on exactly €50.00 of goods (support team).** A customer paid €4.90 for delivery on
+   an order whose goods came to exactly €50.00. The README says shipping is free when the goods come to
+   €50.00 or more, after every discount and before VAT.
+   - Finding: the threshold is already `>=` in `shippingCost` (`src/shipping.ts`), from task-001, and
+     `test/orders.test.ts` already covers exactly €50.00. A randomised check of 20,000 orders, with and
+     without coupons and volume discounts, found no order of €50.00 or more that paid shipping. The
+     charge the customer saw therefore matches an order placed before that fix, or an order whose
+     goods were below €50.00 after discounts. No code change in this task. Support should check the
+     order's date and goods against the README, and any goodwill refund is a decision for the business.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- A single-use coupon used by an order that is then cancelled can be used by a new order.
+- A single-use coupon used by a live order is still refused for another order.
+- A non-single-use coupon is unaffected by cancellation.
+- Goods of exactly €50.00 ship free; €49.99 still pays the band cost (already covered; keep it passing).
+- The existing test suite still passes; a new test covers the cancel-and-reuse case.
